/target

# Vendored crate sources, kept out of the tree.
/.cargo/registry
/.cargo/git

# Reports. The tree carries no report directory: the project dropped the
# earlier one from `main`, and the benchmark harness writes its output here.
# The evidence of a measurement belongs in the commit message, which is in the
# history, and in the file the harness leaves on the machine.
#
# `reports/perf-audit-v0.11.0.md` is the audit of the `perf` commits since
# `v0.11.0`. It stays on the machine and out of the tree.
/reports/

# Store files. `blu backup <dir> <base>` writes `<base>.NNNN.bin` and
# `<base>.vNNNN.idx` into the *current directory* when the base is a bare name,
# and a test that runs the binary without setting a working directory leaves one
# here. `git add -A` will otherwise commit one, and a committed
# `photos.0000.bin` is a 12-byte store header that looks like data.
#
# The command also creates `<base>.lock` while it writes. It deletes that file
# when it closes the lock, so the two rules below cover every file it leaves.
*.[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].bin
*.v[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9].idx
